{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 212 "" 0 "" {TEXT 412 37 "Lecture 6 Procedures a
nd 3x+1 Problem" }}}{SECT 0 {PARA 3 "" 0 "" {TEXT 413 33 "The general \+
syntax of a procedure" }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 48 "The gene
ral syntax of a procedure is as follows:" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 
0 "" }}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 216 4 "name" }{TEXT 414 2 ":=" }{TEXT 
217 4 "proc" }{TEXT 414 17 "(P1, P2, ..., Pn)" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT
 414 3 "   " }{TEXT 218 5 "local" }{TEXT 414 19 " L1, L2, ..., Lu; \n"
 }{TEXT 414 3 "   " }{TEXT 219 6 "global" }{TEXT 414 19 " G1, G2, ...,
 Gv; \n" }{TEXT 414 3 "   " }{TEXT 220 7 "options" }{TEXT 414 19 " O1,
 O2, ..., Ow; \n" }{TEXT 414 3 "   " }{TEXT 221 11 "description" }
{TEXT 414 94 " \"something here to describe the procedure\" (or `somet
hing here to describe the procedure`); \n" }{TEXT 414 11 "       S1;\n
" }{TEXT 414 11 "       S2;\n" }{TEXT 414 10 "      ----" }}{PARA 0 ""
 0 "" {TEXT 414 12 "       Sm; \n" }{TEXT 222 8 "end proc" }{TEXT 414 
1 ";" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 34 
"In the above:                    \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 223 4 "
name" }{TEXT 414 29 " is the name of the procedure" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 414 1 " " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 33 "P1, P2, ..., Pn is a s
equence of " }{TEXT 224 9 "arguments" }{TEXT 414 6 " (aka " }{TEXT 
225 10 "parameters" }{TEXT 414 71 ") that represent the input to the p
rocedure. As we shall see later the " }{TEXT 226 20 "type of a paramet
er." }{TEXT 414 3 " P " }{TEXT 227 69 "may be declared by replacing a \+
parameter by an expression of the form" }{TEXT 414 2 " \n" }{TEXT 414 
1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 16 "             P::" }{TEXT 228 4 "type" }{TEXT 
414 3 ", \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 28 "for example, we could ha
ve \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 12 "        P1::" }{TEXT 229 7 "in
teger" }{TEXT 414 6 ", P2::" }{TEXT 230 6 "matrix" }{TEXT 414 6 ", P3:
:" }{TEXT 231 7 "numeric" }{TEXT 414 7 ", etc.\n" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 414 187 "This means, for example,  that the parameter P1 must be
 an integer, if it is not you will get a warning message when you atte
mpt to use the procedure. Examples below will make this clear." }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 40 "L1, L2, ..., Lu repres
ent a sequence of " }{TEXT 232 5 "local" }{TEXT 414 12 " variables.\n"
 }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 40 "G1, G2, ..., Gv represent a sequence
 of " }{TEXT 233 6 "global" }{TEXT 414 12 " variables.\n" }{TEXT 414 
1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 42 "O1, O2, ..., Ow represent options such as " }
{TEXT 234 6 "trace " }{TEXT 414 3 "and" }{TEXT 235 10 " remember." }
{TEXT 414 32 "   We will discuss these below.\n" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 414 6 "After " }{TEXT 236 11 "description" }{TEXT 414 107 " you \+
may write anything enclosed in \"   \". This is to help document what \+
the purpose of the procedure is. \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 41 "
S1; S2; ... , Sm represent a sequence of " }{TEXT 237 10 "statements" 
}{TEXT 414 67 " which tell the procedure what to do. These may or may \+
not contain " }{TEXT 238 6 "return" }{TEXT 414 56 " statements which p
rovide the output of the procedure. \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 239 
68 "Note that the last thing to be computed is returned unless previou
s " }{TEXT 240 6 "return" }{TEXT 241 106 " statements are executed. So
 if the output is computed on the last line before end; then that is r
eturned." }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 67 "As we hav
e seen a procedure need not contain all of these elements." }}{PARA 0 
"" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 22 "For more detail
s see ?" }{TEXT 242 9 "procedure" }{TEXT 414 4 ",  ?" }{TEXT 243 7 "op
tions" }{TEXT 414 4 ",  ?" }{TEXT 244 10 "parameters" }{TEXT 414 6 ", \+
etc." }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}}{SECT 0 {PARA 3
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 413 50 "Example of a procedure (member with error warni
ng)" }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 47 "We have seen that Maple ha
s a built-in program " }{TEXT 245 7 "member " }{TEXT 414 104 "to test \+
whether or not x is an element of a list or set. Here we construct suc
h a procedure and call it " }{TEXT 246 6 "Member" }{TEXT 414 41 " to d
istinguish it from Maple's built-in " }{TEXT 247 6 "member" }{TEXT 
414 12 ". Note that " }{TEXT 248 10 "x::integer" }{TEXT 414 41 " decla
res that x must be an integer, and " }{TEXT 249 7 "L::list" }{TEXT 
414 32 " declares that L must be a list." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 34 "Member:=proc(x::integer, L::list)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 
11 "  local i;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 91 "  description \"this procedure ret
urns true if x is an integer, L is a list and x is in L\";\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 29 "  for i from 1 to nops(L) do\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 42 "   \+
 if x = L[i] then return true; end if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "  end do;
\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "  false;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "end proc:\n" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 26 "Now lets see how it works." }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "Member(5,[1,2,3]);" }}{PARA 
11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "I&falseG%*protectedG" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0
 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 12 "Member(5,5);" }}{PARA 207 "" 1 "" {TEXT 415 0 "" 
}{HYPERLNK 415 "Error, invalid input: Member expects its 2nd argument,
 L, to be of type list, but received 5" 4 "http://www.maplesoft.com/su
pport/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20invalid%20input%3A%20Member%
20expects%20its%202nd%20argument,%20L,%20to%20be%20of%20type%20list,%2
0but%20received%205" "" }{TEXT 415 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 22 "Member(5,[1,2,3,4,5]);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 
20 "I%trueG%*protectedG" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 23 "
Member(5, \{1,2,3,4,5\});" }}{PARA 207 "" 1 "" {TEXT 415 0 "" }
{HYPERLNK 415 "Error, invalid input: Member expects its 2nd argument, \+
L, to be of type list, but received \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\}" 4 "http://www.m
aplesoft.com/support/help/errors/view.aspx?path=Error,%20invalid%20inp
ut%3A%20Member%20expects%20its%202nd%20argument,%20L,%20to%20be%20of%2
0type%20list,%20but%20received%20%7B1,%202,%203,%204,%205%7D" "" }
{TEXT 415 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 22 "Member(2.2
,[2.3,2.2]);" }}{PARA 207 "" 1 "" {TEXT 415 0 "" }{HYPERLNK 415 "Error
, invalid input: Member expects its 1st argument, x, to be of type int
eger, but received 2.2" 4 "http://www.maplesoft.com/support/help/error
s/view.aspx?path=Error,%20invalid%20input%3A%20Member%20expects%20its%
201st%20argument,%20x,%20to%20be%20of%20type%20integer,%20but%20receiv
ed%202.2" "" }{TEXT 415 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 126 "
We can correct this by changing Member as follows.  This time we leave
 off the type checking. We do type checking another way:" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "restart:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "
" {MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "Member:=proc(x,Y)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "  local i;\n
" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 96 "  description \"this procedure returns true if x i
s anything, Y is a set or list and x is in Y\";\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 45 " \+
 if not(type(Y, set) or type(Y,list)) then \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 57 "    e
rror \"the second argument must be a set or a list\";\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 
0 10 "  end if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 29 "  for i from 1 to nops(Y) do\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 42 "    if x = Y[i] then return true; end if;\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "  end do;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "  false;\n" }{MPLTEXT 
1 0 9 "end proc:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 34 "Member(
2.2, \{1,2,z,sqrt(2), 2.2\});" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "I%trueG
%*protectedG" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 25 "A:=matrix([
[1,2],[3,4]]);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenam
eG6\"I,TypesettingGI(_syslibGF'6%-I#miGF$6%Q\"AF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,
mathvariantGQ'italicF'-I#moGF$6-Q+~&Assign;~F'/F3Q'normalF'/%&fenceGQ&
falseF'/%*separatorGF=/%)stretchyGF=/%*symmetricGF=/%(largeopGF=/%.mov
ablelimitsGF=/%'accentGF=/%'lspaceGQ&0.0emF'/%'rspaceGFL-I(mfencedGF$6
&-F#6#-I'mtableGF$66-I$mtrGF$6'-I$mtdGF$6(-I#mnGF$6$Q\"1F'F9/%)rowalig
nGQ!F'/%,columnalignGF]o/%+groupalignGF]o/%(rowspanGFjn/%+columnspanGF
jn-Fen6(-Fhn6$Q\"2F'F9F[oF^oF`oFboFdoF[oF^oF`o-FX6'-Fen6(-Fhn6$Q\"3F'F
9F[oF^oF`oFboFdo-Fen6(-Fhn6$Q\"4F'F9F[oF^oF`oFboFdoF[oF^oF`o/%&alignGQ
%axisF'/F\\oQ)baselineF'/F_oQ&rightF'/FaoQ'|frleft|hrF'/%/alignmentsco
