{TEXT 341 19 " dynamical system. " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 4 "The " }{TEXT 342 47 "composition of a fun
ction f with itself n times" }{TEXT 414 25 " is sometimes called the "
 }{TEXT 343 12 "n-th iterate" }{TEXT 414 33 " of f. In Maple it is den
oted by " }{TEXT 344 4 "f@@n" }{TEXT 414 92 ". Recall that if f and g \+
are functions, f@g is the composition of f and g. So, for example, " }
{TEXT 345 36 "(f@@3 )(x) = (f@f@f)(x) = f(f(f(x)))" }{TEXT 414 12 ". N
ote that " }{TEXT 346 13 "(f@@0)(x) = x" }{TEXT 414 25 ". The parenthe
ses around " }{TEXT 347 7 "(f@@3) " }{TEXT 414 11 "are needed." }{TEXT
 348 1 " " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "restart:\n" }}}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 154 "Here  are some procedures that one may \+
use to investigate the dynamics of a given function. First we define a
 function f  that we want to experiment with." }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0
 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 21 "f:=x->(25*x) mod 197;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 ">I\"fG6\"f*6#I\"xGF$F$6$I)operatorGF$I&arrowGF$F$-I$modGF
$6$,$*&\"#D\"\"\"F'F1F1\"$(>F$F$F$" }}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" 
}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 25 "The following procedure, " }
{TEXT 349 3 "it1" }{TEXT 414 38 ",  will produce the list of the first
 " }{TEXT 350 1 "n" }{TEXT 414 28 " iterations of any function " }
{TEXT 351 4 "func" }{TEXT 414 25 " starting with the value " }{TEXT 
352 5 "start" }{TEXT 414 2 ":\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 
1 0 24 "it1:=proc(start,func,n)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "local i;\n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 32 "[seq((func@@i)(start),i=0..n)];\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "
end proc:\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 1 " " }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 
54 "We first see what the output is for undefined g and x:" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "it1(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F#--I#@@G6$%*protectedGI(_syslibGF$6$
F&\"\"#F'--F*6$F&\"\"$F'--F*6$F&\"\"%F'--F*6$F&\"\"&F'" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 37 "Let's try the function defined above." }
}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "it1(1,f,5);" }}{PARA 11 ""
 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "7(\"\"\"\"#D\"#M\"#i\"$r\"\"$Q\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0
 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 13 "it1(1,f,100);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "7aq\"\"\"\"#D\"#M\"#i\"$r\"\"$Q\"\"$,\"\"$h\"\"#&)\"$b\"
\"$K\"\"$[\"\"$a\"\"$2\"\"$9\"\"##*\"$L\"\"$t\"\"$)=\"$p\"\"#))\"#L\"#
P\"$P\"\"#w\"$F\"\"#B\"$\"=\"$\">\"#Z\"$!>\"#A\"$c\"\"$d\"\"$#=\"#>\"#
\")\"#b\"$$>\"#(*\"#h\"$Y\"\"$/\"\"#R\"$(=\"$W\"\"#a\"$o\"\"#j\"$'>\"$
s\"\"$j\"\"$N\"\"#E\"#f\"#'*\"#O\"$7\"\"#U\"#l\"#\\\"#V\"#!*\"#$)\"$0
\"\"#k\"#C\"\"*\"#G\"$4\"\"$k\"\"$g\"\"#g\"$@\"\"#q\"$u\"\"#;\"\"'\"$]
\"\"\"(\"$v\"\"#T\"#S\"#:\"$y\"\"$;\"\"$U\"\"\"%\"$+\"\"$O\"\"#^\"#$*
\"$e\"\"#5\"#`\"$V\"\"#H\"$M\"F#F$F%" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 13 "Note that in " }{TEXT 353 3 "it1" }{TEXT 
414 22 " each computation of  " }{TEXT 354 7 "func@@n" }{TEXT 414 98 "
 starts from the beginning and requires n steps. A better way to write
 the program is as follows:\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 
0 24 "it2:=proc(start,func,n)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 16 " local i,x,SEQ;\n" 
}{MPLTEXT 1 0 11 " x:=start;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 " SEQ:=x; \n" }
{MPLTEXT 1 0 22 " for i from 1 to n do\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 15 "   x:=func
(x);\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 17 "   SEQ:= SEQ, x;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 " end do
;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 8 " [SEQ];\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "end proc:\n" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "it1(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1
 "" {XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F#--I#@@G6$%*protectedGI(_syslibG
F$6$F&\"\"#F'--F*6$F&\"\"$F'--F*6$F&\"\"%F'--F*6$F&\"\"&F'" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "it2(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F#-F&6#F%-F&6#F(-F&6#F*-F&6#F," }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 57 "We can also write a recursive ver
sion of this procedure:\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 
24 "it3:=proc(start,func,n)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 18 " option remember:\n" 
}{MPLTEXT 1 0 35 " if n = 0 then return [start]; fi;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 
64 " return [op(it3(start,func,n-1)),func(it3(start,func,n-1)[n])];\n"
 }{MPLTEXT 1 0 5 "end:\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 
"it3(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F#-F
&6#F%-F&6#F(-F&6#F*-F&6#F," }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 
11 "it1(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F
#--I#@@G6$%*protectedGI(_syslibGF$6$F&\"\"#F'--F*6$F&\"\"$F'--F*6$F&\"
\"%F'--F*6$F&\"\"&F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 11 "it2
(x,g,5);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "7(I\"xG6\"-I\"gGF$6#F#-F&6#F
%-F&6#F(-F&6#F*-F&6#F," }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 75 "Here's
 another way to time a procedure--without getting the output however:"
 }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 19 "time(it1(1,f,300));" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "$\"#$*!\"$" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 19 "time(it2(1,f,300));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "
$\"\"!F#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 17 "For small values " }
{TEXT 355 3 "it3" }{TEXT 414 70 " is fast, but for really large values
 it will require too much memory." }}}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }
}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 19 "time(it3(1,f,300));" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "$\"\"!F#" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}}{SECT 0 {PARA 3 "" 0 "" {TEXT 413 25 "The famous
 3x + 1 problem" }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 210 96 "This is a famo
us open problem in mathematics which involves iteration of a particula
r function.\n" }{TEXT 210 1 "\n" }{TEXT 210 22 "Consider the function 
" }{TEXT 414 1 "f" }{TEXT 210 41 " defined on positive integers by the
 rule" }{TEXT 414 2 " \n" }{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 60 "           \+
                    f(k) = k/2,  if k is even,  \n" }{TEXT 414 59 "   \+
                            f(k) = 3k+1,  if k is odd. \n" }{TEXT 414 
1 " " }{TEXT 210 1 "\n" }{TEXT 210 47 "It appears that if one starts w
ith any integer " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-msub(
Typesetting:-mi(\"n\", italic = \"true\", mathvariant = \"italic\"), T
ypesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mn(\"0\", mathvariant = \"normal\")), su
bscriptshift = \"0\"));" "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenameG6\"I,TypesettingGI(_
syslibGF'6#-I%msubGF$6%-I#miGF$6%Q\"nF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,mathvarian
tGQ'italicF'-F#6#-I#mnGF$6$Q\"0F'/F6Q'normalF'/%/subscriptshiftGF=" }
{TEXT 414 0 "" }{TEXT 210 14 " and iterates " }{TEXT 414 1 "f" }{TEXT 
210 88 ", one always eventually reaches the number 1. This has been ve
rified for many values of " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesetting:-mrow(Typesett
ing:-msub(Typesetting:-mi(\"n\", italic = \"true\", mathvariant = \"it
alic\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mn(\"0\", mathvariant = \"norm
al\")), subscriptshift = \"0\"));" "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenameG6\"I,Types
ettingGI(_syslibGF'6#-I%msubGF$6%-I#miGF$6%Q\"nF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,
mathvariantGQ'italicF'-F#6#-I#mnGF$6$Q\"0F'/F6Q'normalF'/%/subscriptsh
iftGF=" }{TEXT 210 2 ", " }{TEXT 356 40 "but has not yet been proved o
r disproved" }{TEXT 210 22 ". It was verified for " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Ty
pesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-msub(Typesetting:-mi(\"n\", italic = \"tr
ue\", mathvariant = \"italic\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mn(\"0
\", mathvariant = \"normal\")), subscriptshift = \"0\"));" "-I%mrowG6#
/I+modulenameG6\"I,TypesettingGI(_syslibGF'6#-I%msubGF$6%-I#miGF$6%Q\"
nF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,mathvariantGQ'italicF'-F#6#-I#mnGF$6$Q\"0F'/F6
Q'normalF'/%/subscriptshiftGF=" }{TEXT 210 24 " up to approximately  2
*" }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"\"), Typesettin
g:-mrow(Typesetting:-msup(Typesetting:-mn(\"10\", mathvariant = \"norm
al\"), Typesetting:-mn(\"16\", mathvariant = \"normal\"), superscripts
hift = \"0\")), Typesetting:-mi(\"\"));" "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenameG6\"I
,TypesettingGI(_syslibGF'6%-I#miGF$6#Q!F'-F#6#-I%msupGF$6%-I#mnGF$6$Q#
10F'/%,mathvariantGQ'normalF'-F56$Q#16F'F8/%1superscriptshiftGQ\"0F'F+
" }{TEXT 414 0 "" }{TEXT 210 86 " in 1999 and apparently the computer \+
is still running. (Search the internet  for  the " }{TEXT 357 12 "3x+1
 problem" }{TEXT 210 8 " or the " }{TEXT 358 15 "collatz problem" }
{TEXT 210 89 " (as it is sometimes called)--if you want more up-to-dat
e information about the problem.)" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 27 "For example, starting with " }{XPPEDIT 
18 0 "Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Types
etting:-msub(Typesetting:-mi(\"n\", italic = \"true\", mathvariant = \+
\"italic\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mn(\"0\", mathvariant = \"
normal\")), subscriptshift = \"0\"), Typesetting:-mo(\"=\", mathvarian
t = \"normal\", fence = \"false\", separator = \"false\", stretchy = \+
\"false\", symmetric = \"false\", largeop = \"false\", movablelimits =
 \"false\", accent = \"false\", lspace = \"0.2777778em\", rspace = \"0
.2777778em\"), Typesetting:-mn(\"6\", mathvariant = \"normal\")), Type
setting:-mi(\"\"));" "-I%mrowG6#/I+modulenameG6\"I,TypesettingGI(_sysl
ibGF'6%-I#miGF$6#Q!F'-F#6%-I%msubGF$6%-F,6%Q\"nF'/%'italicGQ%trueF'/%,
mathvariantGQ'italicF'-F#6#-I#mnGF$6$Q\"0F'/F;Q'normalF'/%/subscriptsh
iftGFB-I#moGF$6-Q\"=F'FC/%&fenceGQ&falseF'/%*separatorGFM/%)stretchyGF
M/%*symmetricGFM/%(largeopGFM/%.movablelimitsGFM/%'accentGFM/%'lspaceG
Q,0.2777778emF'/%'rspaceGFfn-F@6$Q\"6F'FCF+" }{TEXT 414 9 " we have\n"
 }{TEXT 414 2 " \n" }{TEXT 414 93 "                        f(6)=3, f(3
)=10, f(10)=5, f(5)=16, f(16)=8, f(8)=4, f(4)=2, f(2)=1. \n" }{TEXT 
414 1 "\n" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 210 47 "Thus in 8 steps we reach 1 \+
if we start from 6. " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 
"" {TEXT 414 60 "Let's define a procedure to implement the \"3x + 1 fu
nction\"." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "
" {MPLTEXT 1 0 8 "restart;" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 
11 "f:=proc(n)\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 22 " if n mod 2 = 0 then \n" }{MPLTEXT
 1 0 17 "   return n/2 ; \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 6 " else\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 
17 "  return 3*n+1; \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 " end if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "
end proc:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 37 "Now let's iterate i
t starting with 3:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 30 "S:=[s
eq((f@@n)(3), n=1..10)]; " }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 ">I\"SG6\"7,
\"#5\"\"&\"#;\"\")\"\"%\"\"#\"\"\"F*F+F," }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 414 106 "Note that we quickly reach 1 and then the sequence of i
terates begins repeating 1, 4, 2, 1, 4, 2, 1, . . ." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 29 "We use the bui
ltin procedure " }{TEXT 359 6 "member" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }{TEXT 414 
103 " as follows to determine whether or not and if so what the first \+
value of n is for which (f@@n)(3) = 1:" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "member(1,S,'n'); \n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 2 "n;" }}{PARA 11 
"" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "I%trueG%*protectedG" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 
20 "\"\"(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 81 "This shows that for
 n = 7 we get 1. So 1 is reached starting from 3 in 7 steps. \n" }
{TEXT 414 1 "\n" }{TEXT 414 117 "Let's write a procedure that tells us
 how many steps are required to reach 1 starting with any positive int
eger n0: (" }{TEXT 360 36 "We could use the above method using " }
{TEXT 361 6 "member" }{TEXT 362 5 " and " }{TEXT 363 3 "seq" }{TEXT 
364 102 ", but that's not very efficient and anyhow we don't know how \+
far we might have to go before getting 1." }{TEXT 414 2 ")\n" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 16 "steps:=proc(n0)\n" }{MPLTEXT
 1 0 11 "local x,i;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 35 "  if n0 = 1 then return 0; en
d if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "  x:=n0;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "  for i from 1
 do\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 13 "    x:=f(x);\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 36 "    if x = \+
1 then return i; end if;\n" }{MPLTEXT 1 0 10 "  end do;\n" }{MPLTEXT 
1 0 10 "end proc:\n" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 9 "steps
(3);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "\"\"(" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 ""
 {TEXT 414 23 "Let's see which number " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesetting:-m
