t recursive algorithm for computing integer powers using the minimal n
umber of multiplications. " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 391 3 "(a)" }{TEXT 414 19 " Write a procedure " }{TEXT 
392 6 "MatPow" }{TEXT 414 82 "(X,n::integer) to implement this algorit
hm for computing powers of matrices. Test " }{TEXT 393 6 "MatPow" }
{TEXT 414 23 "(<<1|2>,<3|4>>,12) and " }{TEXT 394 6 "MatPow" }{TEXT 
414 20 "(<<1|2>,<3|4>>,-12)." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 395 3 "(b)" }{TEXT 414 19 " Write a procedure " 
}{TEXT 396 7 "PolyPow" }{TEXT 414 182 "(X,n::integer) to implement thi
s algorithm for computing powers of numbers and polynomials. Your proc
edure needs to exapnd each product of polynomials in order to be effec
tive. Test " }{TEXT 397 7 "PolyPow" }{TEXT 414 10 "(123,12), " }{TEXT 
398 7 "PolyPow" }{TEXT 414 9 "(123,-12)" }{TEXT 399 9 ", PolyPow" }
{TEXT 414 15 "(x^2+1,12) and " }{TEXT 400 7 "PolyPow" }{TEXT 414 13 "(
x^2+1,-12). " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT
 401 9 "Problem 4" }{TEXT 414 3 ".  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 ""
 }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 402 13 "Happy numbers" }{TEXT 414 216 " are p
ositive integers which end up at 1 under iteration of the \"sum of squ
ares of digits map\". That is, if one defines f(x) to be the sum of th
e squares of the decimal digits of  the positive integer x, then  x  i
s " }{TEXT 403 5 "happy" }{TEXT 414 56 " if for some positive integer \+
n we have (f@@n)(x) = 1.  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0
 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 13 "For example, " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 ""
 }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 16 "f(7) = 7^2=49,  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" 
{TEXT 414 21 "f(49) = 4^2+9^2=97,  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 22 "f
(97) = 9^2+7^2=130,  " }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 26 "f(130) = 1^2+3^
2+0^2 = 10," }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 21 "f(10) = 1^2+0^2 = 1. " }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 14 "So 7 is
 happy." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 
33 "The first few happy numbers are \n" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 
61 "1,7,10,13,19,23,28,31,32,44,49,68,70,79,82,86,91,94,97,100. \n" }}
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 414 86 "Write a  procedure that will declare a p
ositive integer  x to be happy (i.e., returns " }{TEXT 404 4 "true" }
{TEXT 414 50 ") if the n-th iterate of f starting with x gives 1" }
{TEXT 405 10 " for some " }{XPPEDIT 18 0 "Typesetting:-mrow(Typesettin
g:-mi(\"\"), Typesetting:-mrow(Typesetting:-mi(\"n\", italic = \"true
\", mathvariant = \"italic\"), Typesetting:-mo(\"&le;\", mathvariant =
